# Hailprint cron entries: one nightly run per day, and one ODIN snapshot every 15 minutes.
# Install after the two path edits below: crontab scripts/hailprint.cron
# `crontab FILE` replaces the whole crontab of this user. Merge by hand when one exists.
# 14:00 UTC: the 12Z file of yesterday's storm date lands on S3 after 12:00 UTC.
# CRON_TZ works on cronie and systemd-cron. Debian cron ignores it: on that host, set the
# system time zone to UTC or write the hour in local time.
# PATH: cron starts with /usr/bin:/bin. uv installs under ~/.local/bin; node and vercel must
# be on this PATH too. Cron expands no variable in this file, so write the home path in full.
# VERCEL_TOKEN, VERCEL_ORG_ID, and VERCEL_PROJECT_ID go in <repo>/.env, never here.
# The ODIN line takes one snapshot of the open outages per quarter hour. It takes no lock and
# writes only data/derived/odin/. ODIN keeps no history, so power data starts at the install.
# shortcut: no log rotation, upgrade to logrotate when the host runs past one year
CRON_TZ=UTC
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/home/<user>/.local/bin
0 14 * * * cd /path/to/hailprint && scripts/nightly.sh >> data/nightly.log 2>&1
*/15 * * * * cd /path/to/hailprint && uv run hailprint odin >> data/odin.log 2>&1
